'''Corrupt''' is a [[Unique Weapons|unique]] knife that was originally given to victims of the [[The Data Loss Glitch (2014)|Data Loss Glitch]].<ref>[https://twitter.com/NikilisRBX/status/549475861079269377 Tweet from @NikilisRBX giving people who lost their inventory an extremely rare knife]</ref> It was originally the 2nd rarest knife in the game (after [[Nik's Scythe]]), before the [[The Duping Glitch (2017)|Duping Glitch of 2017]]. It is now only obtainable through trading. 

==Appearance==
Its blade is golden with minimal vintage designs imprinted on it by the heel. The guard is silver, and the handle is grayish-black.  

== Trivia==
*In the main lobby, the statue of [[Nikilis]] on the water fountain can be seen holding this knife.
*This knife was one of the main targets of [[the Duping Glitch (2017)|The Duping Glitch of 2017]], and lost a massive amount of value after the event.
* This knife was the first [[Unique Weapons|unique weapon]] to ever exist, although this category was initially named "[[Unique Weapons|Reward]]"<ref>[https://twitter.com/NikilisRBX/status/549477066023129088 Tweet from @NikilisRBX confirming a new rarity along with how it was obtained]</ref><ref>[https://twitter.com/NikilisRBX/status/550023176672276480 Tweet from @NikilisRBX talking about the item rarity colors and names]</ref> before being changed to "[[Unique Weapons|Unique]]" following an update later.
*It is the only weapon with a rarity above [[Legendary Weapons|Legendary]] that has the same mesh as the [[Default Knife]].
*This is the only tradable [[Unique Weapons|unique weapon]].
* Owning more than 20 Corrupts will result in the owner's account being banned upon rejoining the game.
*There is also a glitch with Corrupt where you must reset your character before finally obtaining it in your [[inventory]], and it's also the same way around when you trade away a Corrupt. 
*Before it was mass [[Duping|duplicated]], there were (allegedly) only around 63 players who owned this knife in 2015-2017. Now there are thousands of copies of it in the game.
*It partners with the [[Godly Weapons|godly]] gun [[Luger]], making the [[Murder Mystery 2 Wiki:Wiki-Bot/Corrupt Set|Corrupt Set]].



